60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C, the meeting space, is the only one that addresses the core issue of unowned space.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,I vote for C. It gives us a place to have the conversations we avoid.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"I’m torn. The kitchen (A) saves lunch trips, but the meeting space (C) saves our sanity.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The kitchen (A) is cheaper, but the callouts worry me. The meeting space (C) is a better investment.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,The quiet room (B) is impossible due to the wall. It’s between A and C.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, the lunch trip is 25 minutes. A meeting space doesn’t solve that, but it solves the conflict.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Ryuji, exactly. The conflict is the bigger cost. I’m voting C.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, I hear you. But who cleans the meeting room? I don’t want to be the one.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, the shared calendar in Option C governs use. It should include cleanup duties.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Shunichi, a calendar is good. It makes the rules clear. I’m leaning C.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"The shared calendar is key. It prevents the ""first come"" chaos. I’m voting C.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I stand by my vote for C. It’s the only option that fosters connection.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"I’ll vote C, but only if the cleanup is rotated. I can’t do it all.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I vote C. The 141,000 yen is an investment in a functional space, not a liability.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,I vote C. It’s the most rational choice given the sound and mess issues.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
